                <pb facs="0633" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg621"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3780: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-13T20:00:00-03:00">June 13, 1940—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 13—1:57 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>275. My 272, June 11, midnight [<hi rendition="#italic">June 12, 8 p.m.</hi>].
                    The President issued late this afternoon through the Department of Press and
                    Propaganda the statement mentioned which the press associations will carry. He
                    assures me his sentiments have not changed and he is still prepared to cooperate
                    100 percent with us.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
